<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ActionUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>ActionUsage</code> is a <code>Usage</code> that is also a <code>Step</code>, and, so, is typed by a <code>Behavior</code>. Nominally, if the type is an <code>ActionDefinition</code>, an <code>ActionUsage</code> is a <code>Usage</code> of that <code>ActionDefinition</code> within a system. However, other kinds of kernel <code>Behaviors</code> are also allowed, to permit use of <code>Behaviors</code> from the Kernel Model Libraries."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
