<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AllocationDefinitionShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>AllocationDefinition</code> is a <code>ConnectionDefinition</code> that specifies that some or all of the responsibility to realize the intent of the <code>source</code> is allocated to the <code>target</code> instances. Such allocations define mappings across the various structures and hierarchies of a system model, perhaps as a precursor to more rigorous specifications and implementations. An <code>AllocationDefinition</code> can itself be refined using nested <code>allocations</code> that give a finer-grained decomposition of the containing allocation mapping."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AllocationDefinitionShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "AllocationDefinitionShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
