<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssertConstraintUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>AssertConstraintUsage</code> is a <code>ConstraintUsage</code> that is also an <code>Invariant</code> and, so, is asserted to be true (by default). Unless it is the <code>AssertConstraintUsage</code> itself, the asserted <code>ConstraintUsage</code> is related to the <code>AssertConstraintUsage</code> by a ReferenceSubsetting <code>Relationship</code>."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssertConstraintUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "AssertConstraintUsageShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssignmentActionUsageShape> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://open-services.net/ns/core#ResourceShape> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssignmentActionUsageShape> <http://open-services.net/ns/core#describes> <https://www.omg.org/spec/sysml/vocabulary#AssignmentActionUsage> .
