<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssignmentActionUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>AssignmentActionUsage</code> is an <code>ActionUsage</code> that is defined, directly or indirectly, by the <code>ActionDefinition</code> <em><code>AssignmentAction</code></em> from the Systems Model Library. It specifies that the value of the <code>referent</code> <code>Feature</code>, relative to the target given by the result of the <code>targetArgument</code> <code>Expression</code>, should be set to the result of the <code>valueExpression</code>."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/AssignmentActionUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "AssignmentActionUsageShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
