<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/FeatureShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A <code>Feature</code> is a <code>Type</code> that classifies relations between multiple things (in the universe). The domain of the relation is the intersection of the <code>featuringTypes</code> of the <code>Feature</code>. (The domain of a <code>Feature</code> with no <code>featuringTyps</code> is implicitly the most general <code>Type</code> <em><code>Base::Anything</code></em> from the Kernel Semantic Library.) The co-domain of the relation is the intersection of the <code>types</code> of the <code>Feature</code>.\n\n."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/FeatureShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "FeatureShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
