<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/InvocationExpressionShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>InvocationExpression</code> is an <code>InstantiationExpression</code> whose <code>instantiatedType</code> must be a <code>Behavior</code> or a <code>Feature</code> typed by a single <code>Behavior</code> (such as a <code>Step</code>). Each of the input <code>parameters</code> of the <code>instantiatedType</code> are bound to the <code>result</code> of an <code>argument</code> <code>Expression</code>. If the <code>instantiatedType</code> is a <code>Function</code> or a <code>Feature</code> typed by a <code>Function</code>, then the <code>result</code> of the <code>InvocationExpression</code> is the <code>result</code> of the invoked <code>Function</code>. Otherwise, the <code>result</code> is an instance of the <code>instantiatedType</code> (essentially like a behavioral <code>ConstructorExpression</code>)."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/InvocationExpressionShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "InvocationExpressionShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ItemDefinitionShape> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://open-services.net/ns/core#ResourceShape> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ItemDefinitionShape> <http://open-services.net/ns/core#describes> <https://www.omg.org/spec/sysml/vocabulary#ItemDefinition> .
