<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ItemDefinitionShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>ItemDefinition</code> is an <code>OccurrenceDefinition</code> of the <code>Structure</code> of things that may themselves be systems or parts of systems, but may also be things that are acted on by a system or parts of a system, but which do not necessarily perform actions themselves. This includes items that can be exchanged between parts of a system, such as water or electrical signals."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
