<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ItemUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An <code>ItemUsage</code> is a <code>ItemUsage</code> whose <code>definition</code> is a <code>Structure</code>. Nominally, if the <code>definition</code> is an <code>ItemDefinition</code>, an <code>ItemUsage</code> is a <code>ItemUsage</code> of that <code>ItemDefinition</code> within a system. However, other kinds of Kernel <code>Structures</code> are also allowed, to permit use of <code>Structures</code> from the Kernel Model Libraries."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/ItemUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "ItemUsageShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
