<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/MetadataUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A  <code>MetadataUsage</code> is a <code>Usage</code> and a <code>MetadataFeature</code>, used to annotate other <code>Elements</code> in a system model with metadata. As a <code>MetadataFeature</code>, its type must be a <code>Metaclass</code>, which will nominally be a <code>MetadataDefinition</code>. However, any kernel <code>Metaclass</code> is also allowed, to permit use of <code>Metaclasses</code> from the Kernel Model Libraries."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/MetadataUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "MetadataUsageShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
