<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/StateUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A <code>StateUsage</code> is an <code>ActionUsage</code> that is nominally the <code>Usage</code> of a <code>StateDefinition</code>. However, other kinds of kernel <code>Behaviors</code> are also allowed as <code>types</code>, to permit use of <code>Behaviors</code>\n."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
