<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/TransitionUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A <code>TransitionUsage</code> is an <code>ActionUsage</code> representing a triggered transition between <code>ActionUsages</code> or <code>StateUsages</code>. When triggered by a <code>triggerAction</code>, when its <code>guardExpression</code> is true, the <code>TransitionUsage</code> asserts that its <code>source</code> is exited, then its <code>effectAction</code> (if any) is performed, and then its <code>target</code> is entered."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20250201/shapes/TransitionUsageShape> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "TransitionUsageShape"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
